x-probe-001-title = the probe launcher is missing a setting, or a setting is not well-formed
x-probe-001-what = ops/federation/standup/probe-launcher.sh (phase 14's run-owned acceptance probes) refused before it touched the edge host: a setting it needs is not set, a value that goes into a command on the edge host is not of its form, or the call is not one of start, stop and alive with their arguments. The message names the setting.
x-probe-001-cause-1 = FED_PL_SSH (user@address of the edge host) or FED_PL_LOCAL=1 is not set
x-probe-001-cause-2 = FED_PL_REST_IP, FED_PL_FAR_IP, FED_PL_DIR, FED_PL_PORT or FED_PL_PINS is not set, or an address is not one IPv4 address
x-probe-001-cause-3 = FED_PL_REST_IP is 0.0.0.0: the probe's REST port writes as the probe's identity, so it binds to one address
x-probe-001-cause-4 = FED_PL_DIR lacks <kind>-cert.pem, <kind>-key.pem or far-ca.pem for the kind asked
x-probe-001-cause-5 = a stop or alive handle is not one this launcher gave (goat-probe-<kind>-<run>)
x-probe-002-title = the edge host's pins carry no zenoh image pinned by digest
x-probe-002-what = ops/federation/standup/probe-launcher.sh takes the probe's image from the edge host's group_vars pins.yml (FED_PL_PINS), its zenoh_router_image. The file cannot be read, or that value is not an image pinned by @sha256 digest, so no probe was started.
x-probe-002-cause-1 = FED_PL_PINS names another file than the edge host's group_vars/<group>/pins.yml
x-probe-002-cause-2 = the pins are not rendered yet, or zenoh_router_image is a tag or a template expression
x-probe-003-title = a probe session did not answer, or the edge host did not say whether it runs
x-probe-003-what = ops/federation/standup/probe-launcher.sh started a probe and its REST port did not answer within a minute, so the probe was removed and start exited 1; or, on alive, the edge host did not answer, so the launcher exited 2 rather than report the probe gone.
x-probe-003-cause-1 = the probe container could not start: the image is not on the edge host, or its zenoh config was refused
x-probe-003-cause-2 = the probe's REST port is not reachable from where phase 14 runs (a firewall, or FED_PL_REST_IP is not an address of the edge host)
x-probe-003-cause-3 = ssh to the edge host failed (FED_PL_SSH, its key, or sudo)
