gb-338-title = a federation verb faulted (the message names what)
gb-338-what = One of the federation verbs (goatbuilder federate init|lint|compose|diff|verify|apply, run on their own or inside a peering run) stopped on an error its library raised without a catalog code. The library's own refusals carry their codes (X-FED-001 to X-FED-007); this is what is left. goatbuilder prints the library's message unchanged and gives it this code. Nothing after the error ran.
gb-338-cause-1 = the verb's report could not be written: the terminal or the pipe it was sent to closed before the verb finished (for example `goatbuilder federate lint ... | head -1`)
gb-338-cause-2 = a check of the library's own with no code of its own, such as its refusal to sign an acceptance result with the package signer
x-fed-001-title = a federation verb cannot read a file it was given (the message names it)
x-fed-001-what = A federation verb (goatbuilder federate init|lint|compose|diff|verify|apply, or goat federate, which runs the same library) could not read a file it was named: a package, an agreement, a --keyring file or a --signing-key file. The message names the file and the system's reason. Nothing was checked or written.
x-fed-001-cause-1 = the path is mistyped, or the file was never copied to this machine (a partner's package, the composed agreement)
x-fed-001-cause-2 = the file is not readable by this user
x-fed-001-cause-3 = the path names a directory
x-fed-002-title = a federation verb cannot write a file it was asked to write (the message names it)
x-fed-002-what = A federation verb could not write its output: compose or init writing --out, or apply --confirm writing the rendered files under --out <dir>. The message names the file or directory and the system's reason. apply stops at the first file it cannot write; the files before it in its list are written.
x-fed-002-cause-1 = --out names a place that does not exist or is not a directory (a path under a file)
x-fed-002-cause-2 = the directory is not writable by this user, or the disk is full
x-fed-003-title = --now is not a YYYY-MM-DD date
x-fed-003-what = federate compose evaluates the two packages on the date --now gives, a calendar date in UTC written YYYY-MM-DD. The value given is not one. Nothing was composed. Without --now, compose uses today's date in UTC.
x-fed-003-cause-1 = the date has another shape (15/11/2026, 2026-11-15T10:00Z) or is not a real date
x-fed-004-title = a bound key from --key or --keyring cannot be used
x-fed-004-what = federate compose checks each package's signature with the key bound to its sovereign id, given as --key <sovereign_id>=<base64> or in a --keyring file, a JSON object of sovereign_id to base64 key. One of them could not be used: a --key without `=`, a --keyring that is not such an object, or a key that is not a 32-byte Ed25519 public key in base64. Nothing was composed.
x-fed-004-cause-1 = the --key value is missing its <sovereign_id>= part, or its key part was cut short when copied
x-fed-004-cause-2 = the --keyring file is not a JSON object of strings
x-fed-004-cause-3 = the key is not the partner's package key (for example a fingerprint or a private key)
x-fed-005-title = the signing key is not an Ed25519 seed
x-fed-005-what = federate init and verify sign with the file --signing-key names: an Ed25519 seed, as 64 hex characters or as its 32 bytes in base64, alone in the file. The file holds something else. Nothing was signed.
x-fed-005-cause-1 = the file is a PEM key or another key format, not the bare seed
x-fed-005-cause-2 = the file holds a public key, a fingerprint or more than the seed
x-fed-006-title = apply --confirm needs --out
x-fed-006-what = federate apply writes only with --confirm, and only under the directory --out names: it will not choose where to write. --confirm was given without --out, so nothing was written. Without --confirm, apply prints what it would write.
x-fed-006-cause-1 = --out was left out of a command that writes
x-fed-007-title = federate apply cannot tell which party it is
x-fed-007-what = federate apply renders one party's side of an agreement. Without --as it reads the party's sovereign id from this site's declaration, and there is no declaration to read here (no context directory, no declaration file, or one that does not parse). Nothing was rendered.
x-fed-007-cause-1 = --as was left out on a machine that has no federation declaration (federate init writes it)
x-fed-007-cause-2 = the context directory named is not this site's
